{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib proof of the main results of Yau and Yin, \"Delocalization of one-dimensional random band matrices\" (arXiv:2501.01718). The model is the complex Gaussian block band matrix with L blocks of size W, N = WL, and band width W >= N^{1/2+c}. This entry contains Theorem 2.2 (delocalization of the bulk eigenvectors, (2.10)), Theorem 2.3 (the local semicircle law, (2.3)-(2.4)), Theorem 2.4 (quantum diffusion, (2.6)-(2.9)) and Theorem 2.5 (quantum unique ergodicity, (2.12)-(2.13)); they have no hypotheses other than their parameters, and no result of another work is assumed for them. The library also proves Theorem 2.6 (bulk universality) from one external input, stated as an explicit hypothesis; that theorem is not part of this entry.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Jun Yin"
    }
  ],
